positional arguments:
  {doctor,start-intake,check-intake,prepare,validate-handoff,validate-project,migrate-project,status,next,verify,complete,block,resume,stage-status,prepare-stage-approval,prepare-active-stage-plan,plan-active-stage,resume-stage-gate,assess-maturity,accept-stage,level-up,start-maintenance,cancel-maintenance,demo}
    doctor              Validate distribution registries, schemas, skills and
                        manifest.
    start-intake        Create an external provisional intake workspace
                        without modifying the target repository.
    check-intake        Validate PROJECT_INPUT.yaml and regenerate missing
                        questions/readiness.
    prepare             Compile a validated Codex Handoff ZIP from an approved
                        intake workspace.
    validate-handoff    Validate an immutable initial handoff directory or
                        ZIP, including its baseline manifest.
    validate-project    Validate mutable project state after Codex execution
                        without enforcing the original handoff manifest.
    migrate-project     Migrate an extracted v0.4.1 project to v0.5.0 without
                        rewriting immutable history.
    status              Show persisted project/task/run state.
    next                Return or JIT-compile the current READY task bundle.
    verify              Independently check actual writes, expected paths and
                        declared verification commands.
    complete            Accept a PASS-verified Agent Task Result and
                        transition to the next task.
    block               Record a material blocker and safe recovery routes.
    resume              Resolve an OPEN blocker and compile a new run attempt.
    stage-status        Show persisted target, active, observed and accepted
                        implementation levels.
    prepare-stage-approval
                        Write a deterministic exact-bound Stage approval draft
                        without approving or mutating the Stage.
    prepare-active-stage-plan
                        Write a read-only exact-bound draft for the next
                        active Stage, without activating Tasks.
    plan-active-stage   Governed application of a reviewed, exact-bound active
                        Stage work plan.
    resume-stage-gate   Revalidate and recover only a persisted Stage Gate
                        blocker.
